        "detected_claims": [
          {
            "categories": [
              "legal"
            ],
            "statement": "Establishing prayer means keeping it faithfully, with its required acts and conditions, rather than merely performing a gesture from time to time.",
            "proposition": "",
            "source": "",
            "source_reference": "2:43",
            "source_fingerprint": "",
            "source_excerpt": "",
            "support": "pending",
            "rationale": ""
          },
          {
            "categories": [
              "legal"
            ],
            "statement": "Respect for earlier revelation is not a reason to refuse the worship now required.",
            "proposition": "",
            "source": "",
            "source_reference": "2:43",
            "source_fingerprint": "",
            "source_excerpt": "",
            "support": "pending",
            "rationale": ""
          },
          {
            "categories": [
              "legal"
            ],
            "statement": "The present command is thus best understood through the worship and company required, rather than a sweeping claim that no earlier prophet’s followers ever bowed.",
            "proposition": "",
            "source": "",
            "source_reference": "2:43",
            "source_fingerprint": "",
            "source_excerpt": "",
            "support": "pending",
            "rationale": ""
          },
          {
            "categories": [
              "legal"
            ],
            "statement": "The legal weight of congregational prayer also depends on the Prophet’s teaching.",
            "proposition": "",
            "source": "",
            "source_reference": "2:43",
            "source_fingerprint": "",
            "source_excerpt": "",
            "support": "pending",
            "rationale": ""
          },
          {
            "categories": [
              "legal"
            ],
            "statement": "In Aḥmad’s ruling, each man able to attend must do so.",
            "proposition": "",
            "source": "",
            "source_reference": "2:43",
            "source_fingerprint": "",
            "source_excerpt": "",
            "support": "pending",
            "rationale": ""
          },
          {
            "categories": [
              "legal"
            ],
            "statement": "This duty for able men without a valid excuse is adopted here, because the instruction to answer the call is direct.",
            "proposition": "",
            "source": "",
            "source_reference": "2:43",
            "source_fingerprint": "",
            "source_excerpt": "",
            "support": "pending",
            "rationale": ""
          },
          {
            "categories": [
              "legal"
            ],
            "statement": "This need not make every prayer offered alone invalid.",
            "proposition": "",
            "source": "",
            "source_reference": "2:43",
            "source_fingerprint": "",
            "source_excerpt": "",
            "support": "pending",
            "rationale": ""
          },
          {
            "categories": [
              "legal"
            ],
            "statement": "Being bound to attend is one issue; whether a prayer offered alone is valid is another.",
            "proposition": "",
            "source": "",
            "source_reference": "2:43",
            "source_fingerprint": "",
            "source_excerpt": "",
            "support": "pending",
            "rationale": ""
          }
        ],
