      "transmitted_evidence": [
        {
          "statement": "Qatādah identifies prayer and the alms due beside it as two binding duties.",
          "proposition": "",
          "source": "",
          "source_reference": "2:43",
          "source_fingerprint": "",
          "source_excerpt": "",
          "support": "pending",
          "rationale": ""
        },
        {
          "statement": "In the account from Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ carried by al-Nasāʾī, the Prophet sends a man back to repeat a prayer that he has not performed properly.",
          "proposition": "",
          "source": "",
          "source_reference": "2:43",
          "source_fingerprint": "",
          "source_excerpt": "",
          "support": "pending",
          "rationale": ""
        },
        {
          "statement": "In al-Bukhārī, Ibn ʿUmar reports that the Prophet set a tenth on crops watered by rain or natural sources, and half that rate on crops watered by irrigation.",
          "proposition": "",
          "source": "",
          "source_reference": "2:43",
          "source_fingerprint": "",
          "source_excerpt": "",
          "support": "pending",
          "rationale": ""
        },
        {
          "statement": "Muqātil understands the address as calling the People of the Book to pray with Muhammad and his Companions.",
          "proposition": "",
          "source": "",
          "source_reference": "2:43",
          "source_fingerprint": "",
          "source_excerpt": "",
          "support": "pending",
          "rationale": ""
        },
        {
          "statement": "In Aḥmad’s ruling, each man able to attend must do so.",
          "proposition": "",
          "source": "",
          "source_reference": "2:43",
          "source_fingerprint": "",
          "source_excerpt": "",
          "support": "pending",
          "rationale": ""
        },
        {
          "statement": "In Muslim’s report from Abū Hurayrah, a blind man seeks permission to pray at home because he has no guide; after learning that he hears the call, the Prophet tells him to attend.",
          "proposition": "",
          "source": "",
          "source_reference": "2:43",
          "source_fingerprint": "",
          "source_excerpt": "",
          "support": "pending",
          "rationale": ""
        },
        {
          "statement": "The strongly urged practice reading instead stresses the report from Ibn ʿUmar in Muslim that prayer together exceeds prayer alone by twenty-seven degrees.",
          "proposition": "",
          "source": "",
          "source_reference": "2:43",
          "source_fingerprint": "",
          "source_excerpt": "",
          "support": "pending",
          "rationale": ""
        },
        {
          "statement": "In al-Bukhārī, Ibn ʿUmar relates that Sālim, the freedman of Abū Ḥudhayfah, led the early emigrants in prayer because he knew more of the Quran.",
          "proposition": "",
          "source": "",
          "source_reference": "2:43",
          "source_fingerprint": "",
          "source_excerpt": "",
          "support": "pending",
          "rationale": ""
        },
        {
          "statement": "The warning in al-Bukhārī and Muslim against raising the head before the imam makes that discipline serious.",
          "proposition": "",
          "source": "",
          "source_reference": "2:43",
          "source_fingerprint": "",
          "source_excerpt": "",
          "support": "pending",
          "rationale": ""
        }
